A||||5||V8Fiero||V8 Cooling question.........||||5||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||07-16-2000||12:18 AM||||Im currently working on hooking up my radiator hoses etc. to my engine. My question is this. Im going to put an inline filler in the hose that goes to the top of the manifold. This filler will also need to have a radiator cap used with it. Do I have to use the overflow provision that is on the filler piece? I want to use this setup to make it easier for me to fill and purge the system of air. Has anyone used this setup before? Perhaps someone has a better setup than this? <BR>TIA<BR>Scott||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||07-16-2000||06:59 AM||||I have a street rod version of what you're describing on my 36 Ford truck. Of course, I'm using the overflow since that's the only one. Since the Fiero already has the overflow and catch bottle up front, just use a cap that is higher pressure than the radiator cap up front and chances are it'll be ok.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||07-16-2000||02:15 PM||||Plug the overflow outlet that is in the front.<BR>I used a new filler neck for race cars that bolts to the engine.<BR>I have since replaced the clear hose that came with overflow tank with fuel hose.  <BR>The clear hose got too hot and lost its integrity. <BR>You will want to do something similar to this install.<BR>It puts the overflow where it is at the highest point so it will purge the air better.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/mountg1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/motorstrtch.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 07-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Fiero||07-16-2000||07:31 PM||||What about the radiator caps then if I move the purge tank to the back? which one would I want to have the higher pressure?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fsrowsell||07-16-2000||08:09 PM||||This what I had to do, because I first did it the wrong way. The first setup that I did was I keep the Overflow bottle up front and used the inline fill neck in the engine complartment to fill the engine up with coolent. I soon learned that would not work, because the overflow bottle up front would fill up and over flow. So I had to move it in the back and use a higher pressure cap up front and a lower one in the back. that works great for me. My fill nick is in the hose going to the goose neck.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Lou Christopher||07-16-2000||10:49 PM||||I have not tried one yet but Denedbear makes a special filler for small & large block chev that is supposed to purge air, and give you a visible water level gauge. About $139.  Do not know if it is a rip off or good.  Does anyone know what it is or has anyone any experience with it.<BR>                   Lou Christopher<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
